0 1 1-1.06-1.06z" style="fill-opacity:1"/><path fill="currentColor" d="M6.943 2.707c1.704-1.704 4.441-1.672 6.232.118 1.787 1.788 1.821 4.52.125 6.225l-.833.856a.75.75 0 0 1-1.076-1.047l.834-.855.007-.008c1.087-1.087 1.118-2.874-.118-4.11s-3.024-1.206-4.11-.12l-.007.007-.857.834a.75.75 0 0 1-1.046-1.074z" style="fill-opacity:1"/></svg></button><!--astro:end--></astro-island> </div> </header> <div class="*:first:mt-0">  <article> <div class="system-card-richtext"><p>We further evaluate the robustness of the models to jailbreaks:
adversarial prompts that purposely try to circumvent model refusals for
content it’s not supposed to produce. We evaluate using the following
approach:</p></div><ul class="system-card-list"><li class="text-primary-100"><p>StrongReject <span class="citation" data-cites="souly2024strongreject">[<a class="citation-link" data-cite="souly2024strongreject" href="/gpt-5-sensitive-conversations/references#ref-souly2024strongreject" title="Alexandra Souly, Qingyuan Lu, Dillon Bowen, Tu Trinh, Elvis Hsieh, Sana Pandey, et al. A strongreject for empty jailbreaks. arXiv preprint arXiv:2402.10260 ." aria-label="Reference 1: Alexandra Souly, Qingyuan Lu, Dillon Bowen, Tu Trinh, Elvis Hsieh, Sana Pandey, et al. A strongreject for empty jailbreaks. arXiv preprint arXiv:2402.10260 .">1</a>]</span>: inserts a known jailbreak
into an example from the above safety refusal eval. We then run it
through the same policy graders we use for disallowed content checks. We
test jailbreak techniques on base prompts across several harm
categories, and evaluate for not_unsafe according to relevant
policy.</p></li></ul> </article><article id="tbl-2" class="scroll-mt-[max(6rem,calc(var(--site-nav-sticky-offset)_+_var(--system-card-banner-h,0px)_+_var(--system-card-toc-offset,0px)))] md:scroll-mt-[max(6rem,calc(var(--site-nav-sticky-offset)_+_var(--system-card-banner-h,0px)))] not-prose my-12" aria-labelledby="tbl-2-heading" data-block data-block-ref="tbl-2" data-block-section="jailbreaks" tabindex="-1"> <div class="not-prose mb-2xs flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2xs md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-between"> <h3 id="tbl-2-heading" class="text-h4 min-w-0 font-normal text-primary-100 md:flex-1"> Table 2: Jailbreak evaluations </h3> <div class="shrink-0 self-start"> <astro-island uid="Z10yxo9" component-url="/_astro/BlockActions.BmUAId7m.js" component-export="default" renderer-url="/_astro/client.P6ud_8Vb.js" props="{&quot;blockId&quot;:[0,&quot;tbl-2&quot;],&quot;chartId&quot;:[0,null],&quot;copyHref&quot;:[0,&quot;/gpt-5-sensitive-conversations/jailbreaks/tbl-2&quot;],&quot;figureHref&quot;:[0,null],&quot;figureKind&quot;:[0]}" ssr client="load" opts="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;BlockActions&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:true}" await-children><div class="flex items-center gap-4xs"><button type="button" aria-label="Copy permalink" title="Copy permalink" data-analytics-id="copy-permalink" class="flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-full border border-primary-12 text-primary-80 transition hover:bg-primary-4 hover:text-primary-60 focus:outline focus:outline-2 focus:outline-primary-44"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M3.534 6.094A.75.75 0 0 1 4.608 7.14l-.834.857-.006.007c-1.086 1.086-1.119 2.874.118 4.11 1.236 1.236 3.023 1.205 4.11.118l.008-.007.855-.834a.75.75 0 0 1 1.047 1.076l-.856.832c-1.705 1.697-4.437 1.663-6.225-.124-1.788-1.788-1.821-4.52-.124-6.225z" style="fill-opacity:1"/><path fill="currentColor" d="M9.47 5.47a.75.75 0 0 1 1